Rāma recalls the bride-price promise to Kekaya --- Rāma recalls Kaikeyī's two war boons --- Rāma owns his fourteen-year forest charge --- Rāma bids Bharata crown himself and free their father --- Rāma cites Gayā on sons saving fathers --- Rāma sends Bharata to please Ayodhyā --- Rāma claims kingship of wild beasts in Daṇḍaka